llow up if needed by 8th July 2026</p><p>- Owner: Bob Duncan / Paul</p><p>---</p><p>## Revenue and Pipeline Risks</p><p>- Anna Campbell and Gary Fraser are both ready to progress to DIP and become active property lookers, but delays in processing create revenue risk and potential client disengagement.</p><p>- 5 overdue tasks represent potential lost conversion opportunities if not actioned promptly.</p><p>- Referral volume from Dalton Y is inconsistent and below target (you noted they &quot;can&#x27;t even get me one a week&quot;).</p><p>- Case progression velocity requires monitoring to prevent pipeline stagnation.</p><p>---</p><p>## Focus for Next Week</p><p>- **Clear all 8 remaining platform tasks by 5th July 2026, prioritising overdue tasks**</p><p>- **Submit DIPs for Anna Campbell and Gary Fraser by 1st July 2026**</p><p>- **Move cases to appropriate nurture workflows where clients are not ready to proceed (e.g. Jimena F)**</p><p>- **Maintain proper case working standards – continue making genuine contact attempts and progressing cases, not just moving tasks forward cosmetically**</p><p>- **Update CRM immediately when client contact fails or cases stall**</p><p>- **Resolve compliance risk cases (Gary First Time Buyer, Karen Ray Financial Services) to prevent regulatory exposure**</p><p>- **Strengthen advice documentation standards** to reduce compliance review requirements, particularly on technical areas such as mortgage into retirement</p><p>- **Progress Dalton Y referral engagement** by sending planned email update and maintaining regular communication cadence</p><p>---</p><p>## Agreed Actions</p><p>| Action | Owner | Deadline |</p><p>|--------|-------|----------|</p><p>| Submit DIP application for Anna Campbell | Paul Banyard | 1st July 2026 |</p><p>| Contact Gary Fraser to complete fact-find and submit DIP | Paul Banyard | 1st July 2026 |</p><p>| Follow up with Jimena F to arrange DIP or move to nurture workflow | Paul Banyard | 2nd July 2026 |</p><p>| Clo